#
# Declarative competency questions authored as slice-resident test-DSL data,
# executed by the native Rust slice-test harness (crates/slicetest), asserted
# lane. The two cells pin the questions the documentation slice exists to answer:
# which slice owns a documented term (the record→slice bridge), and is every
# gmeow:DocEvidence node grounded (the fail-fast grounding invariant). Both run
# over the self-describing gmeow:cqDataFile overlay scene.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/documentation/tests/> .

# --- 1. Which slice owns a documented term? (RowsContains + overlay) ----------
# A gmeow:DocumentedTerm names exactly one owning slice; the documentation slice's
# own worked scene documents gmeow:DocEvidence, owned by the documentation slice, so
# that slice IRI is the guaranteed witness. RowsContains keeps the cell stable if the
# scene later documents further terms owned by other slices.
ex:cqDocumentedTermOwner a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/documented-term-owner.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/documented-term.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The documentation surface MUST be able to bridge from a term's documentation record back to the slice that owns the term: gmeow:docOwnerSlice is the record→slice edge that lets the docs group terms by slice and link a term to its slice page. Without it the documentation graph would name records with no path back to the owning vocabulary. The self-describing scene documents gmeow:DocEvidence, owned by the documentation slice, so the documentation slice IRI is the witness." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqDocumentedTermOwnerShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqOwnerRowDocumentation .

ex:cqDocumentedTermOwnerShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "owner" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsContains .

ex:cqOwnerRowDocumentation a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "owner" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documentation> ] .

# --- 2. Is a gmeow:DocEvidence node grounded? (ASK + overlay) -----------------
# The fail-fast grounding invariant, asked positively: the scene MUST demonstrate a
# gmeow:DocEvidence node that carries both a gmeow:docEvidenceKind and at least one
# gmeow:docGroundedBy truthmaker — the grounded discipline downstream authors copy.
ex:cqDocEvidenceGrounded a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/doc-evidence-grounded.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/documented-term.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Proof-carrying documentation demands that every gmeow:DocEvidence node be a claim WITH its grounds: a kind (gmeow:docEvidenceKind) and at least one carrier truthmaker (gmeow:docGroundedBy). An ungrounded evidence node is the doc-layer analogue of a DARK finding. The ASK witnesses that the worked scene holds together as a grounded evidence node." ;
    gmeow:cqExpectAsk true .

# --- 3. Is Full's intent a PROPER subset of Maximal's? (RowsContains, module base) ---
# The derived maturity lattice must place FULL strictly below MAXIMAL: the maximal
# anchor's intent must carry attributes the full anchor does not. The query returns
# the maximal-only dimensions; RowsContains pins one guaranteed witness
# (gmeow:dimAnnotationCoat, a maximal-tier dimension) so the cell stays stable as the
# ladder is extended. The anchors and their intents live in the module base graph, so
# no gmeow:cqDataFile overlay is needed.
ex:cqMaturityLattice a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/maturity-lattice.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The named maturity anchors are distinguished intents inside the Formal-Concept lattice of the coverage incidence, and the ladder MUST be a proper chain: gmeow:docMaturityFull's intent is a strict subset of gmeow:docMaturityMaximal's. The query returns the dimensions maximal requires that full does not; a non-empty result proves Full ⊂ Maximal (proper containment), so the two tiers are genuinely distinct concepts and the maturity order is real rather than a degenerate collapse." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqMaturityLatticeShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqMaturityLatticeRowAnnotationCoat .

ex:cqMaturityLatticeShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "dim" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsContains .

ex:cqMaturityLatticeRowAnnotationCoat a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "dim" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/dimAnnotationCoat> ] .
